   Look at active/idle/waiting connection counts. If `active == maximumPoolSize` and threads are waiting, you have pool exhaustion; if the pool is small for the request volume, tune `maximumPoolSize` carefully instead of increasing it blindly. HikariCP’s pool-sizing guidance emphasizes that connection pools are frequently misconfigured and that smaller, well-sized pools often perform better. ([github.com](https://github.com/brettwooldridge/HikariCP/wiki/About-Pool-Sizing))

